{"results":[{"entryType":"UniProtKB reviewed (Swiss-Prot)","primaryAccession":"Q6UXH0","secondaryAccessions":["Q9NQZ1"],"uniProtkbId":"ANGL8_HUMAN","entryAudit":{"firstPublicDate":"2008-02-26","lastAnnotationUpdateDate":"2026-09-02","lastSequenceUpdateDate":"2004-07-05","entryVersion":129,"sequenceVersion":1},"annotationScore":5.0,"organism":{"scientificName":"Homo sapiens","commonName":"Human","taxonId":9606,"lineage":["Eukaryota","Metazoa","Chordata","Craniata","Vertebrata","Euteleostomi","Mammalia","Eutheria","Euarchontoglires","Primates","Haplorrhini","Catarrhini","Hominidae","Homo"]},"proteinExistence":"1: Evidence at protein level","proteinDescription":{"recommendedName":{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:24933"}],"value":"Angiopoietin-like protein 8"}},"alternativeNames":[{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"25417115"}],"value":"Betatrophin"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"22809513"}],"value":"Lipasin"}},{"fullName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"22569073"}],"value":"Refeeding-induced fat and liver protein"}}],"flag":"Precursor"},"genes":[{"geneName":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000312","source":"HGNC","id":"HGNC:24933"}],"value":"ANGPTL8"},"synonyms":[{"value":"C19orf80"},{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"22569073"}],"value":"RIFL"}],"orfNames":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"12975309"}],"value":"UNQ599/PRO1185"}]}],"comments":[{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000250","source":"UniProtKB","id":"Q8R1L8"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22569073"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22809513"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23150577"}],"value":"Hormone that acts as a blood lipid regulator by regulating serum triglyceride levels (PubMed:22569073, PubMed:22809513, PubMed:23150577). May be involved in the metabolic transition between fasting and refeeding: required to direct fatty acids to adipose tissue for storage in the fed state (By similarity)"}],"commentType":"FUNCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23150577"}],"value":"Interacts with ANGPTL3"}],"commentType":"SUBUNIT"},{"commentType":"INTERACTION","interactions":[{"interactantOne":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q6UXH0","intActId":"EBI-3943039"},"interactantTwo":{"uniProtKBAccession":"Q96PM5","geneName":"RCHY1","intActId":"EBI-947779"},"numberOfExperiments":2,"organismDiffer":false}]},{"commentType":"SUBCELLULAR LOCATION","subcellularLocations":[{"location":{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23150577"}],"value":"Secreted","id":"SL-0243"}}]},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22569073"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22809513"}],"value":"Predominantly expressed in liver. Also expressed in adipose tissues"}],"commentType":"TISSUE SPECIFICITY"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22569073"}],"value":"Transcripts are up-regulated by 100 fold during adipogenesis"}],"commentType":"DEVELOPMENTAL STAGE"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"22569073"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"23150577"}],"value":"In response to food intake. Stimulated by insulin"}],"commentType":"INDUCTION"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000303","source":"PubMed","id":"25099942"}],"value":"Proteolytically cleaved at the N-terminus"}],"commentType":"PTM"},{"commentType":"DISEASE","disease":{"diseaseId":"Type 1 diabetes mellitus","diseaseAccession":"DI-01826","acronym":"T1D","description":"A multifactorial disorder of glucose homeostasis that is characterized by susceptibility to ketoacidosis in the absence of insulin therapy. Clinical features are polydipsia, polyphagia and polyuria which result from hyperglycemia-induced osmotic diuresis and secondary thirst. These derangements result in long-term complications that affect the eyes, kidneys, nerves, and blood vessels.","diseaseCrossReference":{"database":"MIM","id":"222100"},"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"24078058"}]},"note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"24078058"}],"value":"The gene represented in this entry may be involved in disease pathogenesis. Increased protein levels are observed in the serum of patients. This result should however be reinvestigated in light of recent advances that suggest that this protein is not promoting pancreatic beta cell proliferation"}]}},{"commentType":"DISEASE","disease":{"diseaseId":"Type 2 diabetes mellitus","diseaseAccession":"DI-02060","acronym":"T2D","description":"A multifactorial disorder of glucose homeostasis caused by a lack of sensitivity to insulin. Affected individuals usually have an obese body habitus and manifestations of a metabolic syndrome characterized by diabetes, insulin resistance, hypertension and hypertriglyceridemia. The disease results in long-term complications that affect the eyes, kidneys, nerves, and blood vessels.","diseaseCrossReference":{"database":"MIM","id":"125853"},"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"24852694"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"24963292"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"25024395"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"25303484"}]},"note":{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"24852694"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"24963292"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"25024395"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"25050901"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"25099942"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"25303484"}],"value":"The gene represented in this entry may be involved in disease pathogenesis. Increased protein levels are observed in the serum of patients and are associated with insulin resistance (PubMed:24852694, PubMed:24963292, PubMed:25024395, PubMed:25303484). According to another report, protein levels are decreased in the serum of patients (PubMed:25050901). Discrepancies between increased and decreased levels of proteins levels in T2D patients may be explained by the use of different kits developed on the market that either use antibodies recognizing the N-terminal or the C-terminal part of the protein (PubMed:25099942). These results should however be reinvestigated in light of recent advances that suggest that this protein is not promoting pancreatic beta cell proliferation"}]}},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}],"value":"Belongs to the ANGPTL8 family"}],"commentType":"SIMILARITY"},{"texts":[{"evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000269","source":"PubMed","id":"25417115"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"23623304"},{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305","source":"PubMed","id":"28038792"}],"value":"Initially reported to specifically promote pancreatic beta cell proliferation without insulin resistance and to promote beta cell mass expansion, thereby improving glucose tolerance (PubMed:23623304). However, this result could not be confirmed by further studies and the original paper was later retracted (PubMed:28038792). The lack of a role in beta cell proliferation was also confirmed in another study (PubMed:25417115)"}],"commentType":"CAUTION"},{"commentType":"SEQUENCE CAUTION","sequenceCautionType":"Erroneous initiation","sequence":"AAF76204.2","note":"Extended N-terminus.","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"ECO:0000305"}]},{"commentType":"SEQUENCE CAUTION","sequenceCautionType":"Erroneous gene model prediction","sequence":"EAW84186.1","evidences":[{"evidenceCode":"E